1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:11,300
Computer vision tracks every player in view from one broadcast camera.

2
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,800
A pass model we trained prices the passes; a published xG model prices the shots.

3
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:22,300
An AI newsroom on Microsoft Agent Framework fact-checks every line before air.

4
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,300
1,306 of 1,306 on-screen numbers checked against the data.

5
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,800
Not built yet: an Azure AI Foundry deployment, live stadium feeds, more trained models.

6
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:34,900
Man Utd v Man City: every option priced live, the danger zone tracked.

7
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,800
Amad shoots from here: 0.06 xG.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,300
The pass to Mbeumo, arriving 84% of the time, was worth 0.11.

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:51,700
Behind the line: agents flag it, price it, draft it, check every number, put it on air.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,900
Arsenal win it back, Saka finds Eze, and their danger-zone share climbs.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,200
Eze from 16 m: 0.08 xG. Saved.

12
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:08,900
Liverpool v Man City, 86th minute: the pass options re-price as the play moves.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,200
Szoboszlai shoots from 29 m: 0.02 xG. Blocked.

14
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:24,600
Mbeumo from 15 m: 0.10 xG.

15
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:34,700
Stoppage time: City keep the ball, and their share of the danger zone creeps up.

16
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:37,200
Then Man Utd break: Cunha on the ball, Mount the best option.

